Backport reproducible image support from squashfs-tools 4.4 to 3.4.

Upstream: https://github.com/plougher/squashfs-tools
Fragment ordering: 24da0c63c80be64e1adc3f24c27459ebe18a19af
Uncompressed flag: 6cd66c6
Time options: 828888d, d1a546a, a033a3e, 7fa76a2, 7db33c9

Reproducible ordering is disabled by default; enable with -reproducible.
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH fixes mkfs_time and clamps inode timestamps;
-mkfs-time sets the creation time and -all-time forces inode timestamps.
Adapt the 4.4 fragment barrier and ordered output to 3.4 queues/caches.
Use independent reorder state and a separate compressed-fragment cache
to avoid blocking behind buffered file data.  Reserve each output buffer
before dequeueing a fragment so small queues cannot block earlier items.
Assign inode numbers after sorting, independently of host readdir order.
Include the ordering thread in the existing append/restore handling.

